{
  "info": {
    "name": "Civicon \u2014 Auth & Identity",
    "description": "Authentication and role-aware identity for the Civicon backend.\n\n## Before you run this\n\n```bash\ndocker compose up -d   # MongoDB\nnpm run seed           # demo accounts, one per role\nnpm run start          # http://localhost:9000\n```\n\n## How it works\n\nEvery route requires a bearer token unless marked `@Public()`. Both `register` and `login` return `{ token, user }`; the token's claims carry the user's roles, so guards need no database round-trip, while `GET /auth/me` re-reads the database and is authoritative when roles have changed since the token was issued.\n\nCollection-level auth is `Bearer {{token}}`, and the sign-in requests populate that variable through their test scripts \u2014 so run a login first and everything else just works.\n\n## Folders\n\n- **Public** \u2014 the only routes reachable without a token\n- **Auth** \u2014 sign-up, sign-in, and who-am-I\n- **Users (admin only)** \u2014 administration; self-contained and safe to run end-to-end\n- **Guardrails** \u2014 the security properties, each asserting its status code. Run this folder as a regression suite.\n\nRoles: `CITIZEN`, `VOLUNTEER`, `AGENCY`, `SPONSOR`, `ADMIN`. Only the first two are self-serve.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:9000",
      "description": "PORT defaults to 9000 in .env.example."
    },
    {
      "key": "demo_password",
      "value": "Password123!",
      "description": "Shared by every account created by `npm run seed`."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically by any sign-in request."
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by register/login."
    },
    {
      "key": "admin_token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by 'Sign in as admin'."
    },
    {
      "key": "citizen_token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by 'Sign in as citizen'."
    },
    {
      "key": "target_user_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by 'Create a disposable user'."
    },
    {
      "key": "wrong_password_message",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Used to prove the 401 messages are identical."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Public",
      "description": "The only routes reachable without a token. Everything else returns 401 \u2014 the guards are registered globally, so a route is protected unless it opts out with @Public().",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Marked @Public() in app.controller.ts.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
